WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.080
The age of menopause is only
partly determined by genetics.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.600
So, what about the
influence of lifestyle factors?

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.340
Watch the video to find out.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:15.660
"How to Delay the Age of Menopause
with Diet and Lifestyle Factors"

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.040
Since 1970,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.120
the proportion of women having
their first child after age 35

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.160
increased nearly tenfold.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.540
This may introduce a "longevity
penalty" on their children,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.440
as those born to older mothers
don't tend to live as long,

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.480
but mothers
having children later

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.880
tend to live longer themselves.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.980
For example,
female centenarians

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.380
were found to be
nearly four times more likely

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.880
to have had children
after age 40

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.460
than women
who died by their 70s.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.340
This doesn't necessarily mean

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.100
delaying kids
will make you live longer.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.740
Smoking, for example,
could be a confounder,

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.980
causing both early menopause
and an early death.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.320
Or maybe
delayed reproductive aging

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.480
is just a sign
of slower aging in general.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.100
However some have suggested the
biological changes of pregnancy

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.020
might have
a rejuvenating effect,

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.040
even going so far as to suggest
that parabiosis mechanism,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.900
bathing in the blood of babies,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.200
but just not in
a Countess Bathory sort of way.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.840
To sort between
these possibilities,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.000
researchers studied
the longevity

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.240
of brothers of women
who gave birth after age 45,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.980
and that of their wives.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.880
The brothers with late-fertile
sisters lived longer,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.620
but their wives did not.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.940
This suggests
a genetic robustness cause,

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.100
rather than
a rejuvenation effect,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.140
and the fact
that the longevity benefit

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.520
didn't extend to their wives

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.440
suggests it's not due
to a confounder

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.360
like socioeconomic strata.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:46.920
On the other hand,

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.220
women who experience
extremely early menopause,

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.220
the 1% who stop menstruating
by age 39,

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.520
may be at risk
for diminished longevity,

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.320
and should
therefore be counseled

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.080
to adopt a particularly
healthy diet and lifestyle.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.320
Approximately half
of the variability

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.120
of age of menopause
between women

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.220
is explained by genetics.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.260
Other than smoking,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.780
what other behaviors
or circumstances

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.340
can help explain the rest?

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.380
Factors that don't appear
to affect the age of menopause

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:24.360
include exercise, obesity,
alcohol, coffee,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.180
or vitamin D status.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.540
Interestingly,
women who've been married

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.120
tend to arrive
at menopause later.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.780
Some suggested it may be the
influence of male pheromones,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.600
given the fact that exposure
to male armpit odor

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.760
makes women's cycles
more regular,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.820
but it turns out
that male cohabitation alone

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.560
doesn't appear to matter.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.140
It may be the sex.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:54.060
Married older individuals tend
to have more sex, and indeed,

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.880
pre- and peri-menopausal women,
average age 46,

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.380
who reported sex weekly

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.860
were 28% less likely
to experience menopause

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.120
over the subsequent decade

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.580
than those reporting sex
less than once a month.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.720
You can very well imagine
how this could be a result

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.940
of reverse causation, though.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.460
Instead of more sex
leading to later menopause,

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.100
a later menopause
may have instead led

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.120
to more sexual engagement.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.440
The relationship between
tobacco use and early menopause

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.120
is thought to be mediated

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.040
by the toxic effects
on the ovaries

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.220
of the polycyclic aromatic
hydrocarbons in the smoke.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.860
Among nonsmokers,

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.300
this PAH exposure
is almost entirely from food,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.700
mostly grilled, barbequed,
and smoked meats.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.380
Could this explain why,

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.360
in the Harvard Nurses'
Health Study II,

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.000
higher plant protein intake
was associated

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.700
with a significantly lower risk
of early menopause?

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.760
Feed female monkeys
a diet high in animal protein

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.280
and not only did they get
more atherosclerosis,

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.580
but also an acceleration
of ovarian aging.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.940
Now, in the original
Harvard Nurses' Health Study,

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.460
animal protein consumption
was associated with infertility,

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.040
such that replacing even 5%

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.960
of animal protein intake
with plant protein

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.420
could potentially cut the risk
of infertility in half.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.700
But in
the Nurses' Health Study II,

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.220
while plant protein
appeared to delay menopause,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.740
animal protein intake
was not associated

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.600
with menopause age
either way.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.940
And in
the UK Women's Cohort Study,

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.380
those eating more animal protein

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.680
were 6% more likely
to experience a later menopause.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.180
The data is similarly
conflicting in vegetarians.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.860
Some studies
found no difference

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.980
or a later age of menopause
in vegetarians,

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.580
but others found an earlier age
compared to nonvegetarians.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.260
For example,
the largest study

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.300
found that vegetarians
reached menopause

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.100
at an average age
of 50.1 years

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:48.180
compared to nonvegetarians
at 50.7 years.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.380
As I noted, premature menopause
before age 40

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.300
may be detrimental
for longevity,

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.420
but being a little earlier
within the normal range

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:01.320
may actually be beneficial
for cancer risk.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:06.540
At the same age, breast cancer
risk is about 40% higher

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.420
in premenopausal compared
to postmenopausal women,

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.640
presumably due
to higher exposure

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.940
to the "necessary evil"
hormone estrogen.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.400
Breast cancer risk
is 3% higher

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.460
for every year later
a woman starts menopause

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.100
and 5% higher
for every year earlier

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.480
a girl starts menstruating.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.260
On average, women whose periods
hold off until age 15

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.700
appear to live the longest.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.300
Vegetarian women tend to have
lower estrogen levels,

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.220
perhaps due
to higher fiber intake,

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.020
and interventional studies show

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.580
that switching
to a more plant-based diet

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.500
can reduce
circulating estrogen levels

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.400
by more than 40%.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.820
This could explain
why vegetarian girls

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.500
may hit puberty later,

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.720
and why those eating
strictly vegetarian

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.880
not only have
lower cancer risk overall,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.300
but particularly lower risk
for female-specific cancers.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.960
Age of menopause
may not be a factor though,

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.940
based on
an interventional trial

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.220
randomizing women
on the verge of menopause,

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.300
average age 49,

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.820
to two years
of a lower fat diet

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.620
to reduce breast cancer risk.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:10.560
The intervention group
ended up eating more fiber,

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.000
and therefore more plant-based,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.280
but though they did
experience improvements

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.540
in mammogram findings,

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.240
the dietary shift
failed to influence

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.860
the timing of menopause.

